Enhancement: Add support for Drime Cloud as a backend

Restic now has a native backend for Drime Cloud. The repository is stored in a
folder hierarchy of the Drime drive and is addressed as `drime:path/to/repo`.
The access token is passed in the `DRIME_ACCESS_TOKEN` environment variable.
The options `drime.workspace-id`, `drime.root-folder-id` and `drime.connections`
can be used to customize the backend. After each upload, the SHA-256 checksum
of the stored file is verified by Drime.

